Melee-NX-NetPlay builds talk to each other (0.4.3): a build message (NP_MSG_NX_BUILD, 0xD0, sent first on the reliable
channel at connection; Slippi Dolphin and melee-unlocked log an unknown id and ignore it) carries the Direct pause rule,
a shield colour and online port colour choices, so between two such builds: Direct pausing can be turned off when
every player's build reads the rule (otherwise Slippi's rule: Start pauses Direct), each sees the other's shield colour,
and a 1v1 shows the players in their chosen port colours (melee-unlocked's rules for all three, its slippi_net.cpp and
slippi_online.cpp). Also melee-unlocked's Unranked skip list (up to three connect codes, blockcode1..3). Against plain
Slippi nothing changes. Applied by ../net_sources.sh after net-0003; port/ is unchanged.
